WEBVTT

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:53.490
Geez, I can't believe he didn't see through the trick.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:55.640
Some people are really retarded.

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:23.170
Don't tell me-

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:25.870
Don't!!!

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:37.840
It was just me?

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:50.890
One per person!

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:52.560
Only one per person!

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:54.410
Here you go.

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:56.570
Where's Oreld?

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:58.370
Oreld?

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:01.740
I'll go find him.

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:04.320
Only one per person.

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:09.120
Oh, come on, what are you doing here?

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:10.280
What do you mean?

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:11.830
I'm doing my job.

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:15.000
Come, come, all women line up over here.

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:18.720
You're pretty cute, so I think I'll give you two sheets.

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:20.550
And you can have my address.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:23.430
I'll be waiting!

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:31.620
O-Oh... Wrong person...

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:32.730
Excuse me...

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:33.940
Ah, sorry, sorry.

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:35.720
Huh?

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:50.010
We're home!

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:50.890
We're back!
We're home!

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:51.750
We're back!

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:53.100
Oreld!

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:54.910
What time do you think it is?

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:57.090
You can only take the girls out for two hours.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:58.740
My bad, my bad.

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:01.050
If anything were to happen to these girls,

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:01.630
how would you compensate me for it?

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:02.670
We bought some sausage, everyone!
how would you compensate me for it?

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:04.230
We bought some sausage, everyone!

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:06.430
Not listening, huh?

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:10.060
I shall be leaving first, then.

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:11.010
Okay.

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:12.770
Have some before you go.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:15.880
She's...

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:20.560
Was she here before?

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:22.120
You mean Hannah?

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:23.700
She's been here.

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:33.460
Welcome.

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:42.380
You coming two days in a row, that's rare.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:45.440
Unfortunately, Mary and Kathy have off today.

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:47.290
Darn, really?

00:04:47.290 --> 00:04:49.320
Then I'll keep myself happy with you, Madam.

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:51.850
Hmph, a little arrogant, aren't we?

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:01.500
Something wrong with Hannah?

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:05.560
Oh, just that she's really been here.

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:07.670
You did say something like that yesterday.

00:05:07.670 --> 00:05:09.790
Is she always like that?

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:12.460
Something about her aura seems different.

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:15.550
It's like she's not really smiling or something.

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:17.480
Perhaps.

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:20.960
She came here when she was only seventeen.

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:25.200
When she lost her parents and had nowhere to go,

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:27.180
the owner here took her under his wing.

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:32.260
Even if it's to survive, this job is too painful for a seventeen-year old girl.

00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:37.600
Also, she's waiting for her boyfriend
who hasn't come back from the war yet.

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:40.850
War? The one with the Republic?

00:05:40.850 --> 00:05:44.320
He was sent to the Neugelitz front four years ago.

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:49.570
His buddies dragged him over here the night before they left.

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:52.110
The guy looked like a kid.

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:53.990
See over there?

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:58.600
Those two just quietly held hands and sat there.

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:17.390
Captain Hunks, coffee for you.

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:22.460
Oreld, let's work hard today.

00:06:23.450 --> 00:06:24.750
Oreld?

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:30.070
Is something wrong with Oreld?

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:32.590
I don't know either.

00:06:32.590 --> 00:06:34.880
He's been like that the entire morning.

00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:40.110
All men, prepare to sortie.

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:43.170
Note: The "Haupt District" is the German analogue to "City Square"
Today's mission is a patrol of the Haupt District.

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:44.270
Yes, sir.

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:46.170
Oreld!

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:47.480
Oreld, are you listening?!

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:48.010
Oreld, she's calling you.
Oreld, are you listening?!

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:49.300
Oreld, she's calling you.

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:50.470
WHAT?!

00:06:50.470 --> 00:06:51.430
WHERE?! WHERE?!

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:54.260
Oh, it's just the LT.

00:06:55.110 --> 00:06:56.970
"It's just the LT"?

00:06:57.390 --> 00:06:58.560
Oreld!

00:06:58.560 --> 00:06:59.100
What's with your attitude?!

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:00.610
C-Calm down, please!
What's with your attitude?!

00:07:00.610 --> 00:07:01.430
You've been too lax this morning!
C-Calm down, please!

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:02.990
You've been too lax this morning!

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:07.060
That's why they all mock us as the cheery unit!

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:07.350
Shape up already, dammit!

00:07:07.350 --> 00:07:09.140
Calm down, please!
Shape up already, dammit!

00:07:09.140 --> 00:07:09.270
Shape up already, dammit!

00:07:09.270 --> 00:07:10.250
Oreld!

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:10.860
Gosh!

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:14.380
You want to take Hannah out?

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:15.200
Yeah.

00:07:17.130 --> 00:07:18.580
Oh, here it is!

00:07:18.820 --> 00:07:22.950
The presentation of this spaghetti may be bad, but the taste is wonderful.

00:07:22.950 --> 00:07:25.090
Sorry if the presentation is bad.

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:33.660
Oh, go ahead and eat.

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:36.920
This is the fork, and this is the spoon.

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:01.870
You didn't enjoy your time with me?

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:04.710
Oh, no, I did.

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:22.080
Here.

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:24.390
I got leftovers today.

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:30.750
Hey.

00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:31.990
Oreld!

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:34.830
What? What are you doing here?

00:08:34.830 --> 00:08:36.080
Just dropping by.

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:37.720
Umm, umm...

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:40.200
Note: "Katzenessen" is German for "cat food"
"Katze Wahnsinn" is German for "Cat Madness"

00:08:41.390 --> 00:08:42.920
Let's eat together?

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:52.320
She's not living.

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:58.490
Oreld said that?!

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:00.810
So something did happen.

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:03.090
You guys really haven't heard anything?

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:06.460
He didn't even tell you?

00:09:06.460 --> 00:09:08.730
Then this must be a rather serious issue.

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:20.500
Why don't we ask him directly?

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:23.610
Ah, but he doesn't feel like talking about it.

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:27.110
He might be waiting for us to ask.

00:09:27.110 --> 00:09:28.580
I'll ask him.

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:29.960
You can't!

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:32.760
If he wants to talk about it, he'll do so himself.

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:35.310
But he seems troubled.

00:09:35.310 --> 00:09:38.300
Let's continue to look after him.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:38.930
Machs!

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:40.230
Yes, sir!

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:45.930
Could I borrow some money?

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:07.770
Stekkin.

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:09.090
Ma-

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:11.850
-chs?

00:10:11.850 --> 00:10:14.220
You couldn't sit still either, huh?

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:15.920
You, too?

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:19.560
Let's go.

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:20.350
Yes, sir.

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:30.060
This is...

00:10:32.970 --> 00:10:33.980
Here he is.

00:10:37.890 --> 00:10:39.490
Where are they going?

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:49.770
What do you think?

00:10:49.770 --> 00:10:50.870
It feels good, right?

00:10:52.850 --> 00:10:54.370
Let's go for another round!

00:11:04.670 --> 00:11:05.760
In love?!

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:07.310
I'm pretty sure of this.

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:12.280
And the girl is an unfortunate call girl who has to sell herself to men in order to survive!

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:15.480
Your form by the window~

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:18.190
~that I see~

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:21.470
For this is an impossible affair~

00:11:21.470 --> 00:11:23.880
Him in love...
For this is an impossible affair~

00:11:23.880 --> 00:11:23.900
The entirety of Section III should support him!
Him in love...

00:11:23.900 --> 00:11:26.910
The entirety of Section III should support him!

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.080
Is Oreld here?

00:11:29.350 --> 00:11:31.910
He took out an army bike without permission!

00:11:31.910 --> 00:11:33.590
The motor pool is furious!

00:11:33.590 --> 00:11:36.170
Sorry, I asked him.

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:38.470
I forgot to file the papers for it.

00:11:39.530 --> 00:11:41.430
So, yeah.

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:42.200
Right?

00:11:53.010 --> 00:11:54.720
It's been a while.

00:11:55.840 --> 00:11:56.810
Come here.

00:12:04.380 --> 00:12:05.950
See? A wonderful scene, right?

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:09.960
The Imperial Army S.S. is over there,

00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:12.330
and the Gelstow district is over there.

00:12:12.850 --> 00:12:16.890
When I don't feel happy, I used to just come here as a kid.

00:12:16.890 --> 00:12:19.380
Just being here makes me feel better.

00:12:22.460 --> 00:12:24.000
I snuck this away from the army.

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:25.480
This drink is good, I tell ya.

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:28.860
Oops, there.

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:38.040
A toast as we watch over the Imperial City.

00:12:38.560 --> 00:12:41.230
Why are you doing so much for me?

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:43.540
Why, you ask?

00:12:44.060 --> 00:12:46.310
Hannah, you were standing on the Mainz Bridge, right?

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:49.510
You had a very sad look on you.

00:12:53.740 --> 00:12:57.530
Just forget him... the guy that went to the war.

00:12:58.300 --> 00:13:02.770
There's no point in thinking about a guy that'll never come back.

00:13:02.770 --> 00:13:05.510
It's not like I don't understand your faith in him, but...

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:07.890
It's been three years since the war ended...

00:13:08.330 --> 00:13:09.220
...and if he were alive, he'd be back already-

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:10.220
Frank will come back!
...and if he were alive, he'd be back already-

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:10.810
Frank will come back!

00:13:12.670 --> 00:13:14.370
Frank will come back.

00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:16.690
He promised me he would.

00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:18.960
That may be, but...

00:13:19.510 --> 00:13:20.810
At this rate, you'll-

00:13:20.810 --> 00:13:22.600
Just leave me alone.

00:13:37.520 --> 00:13:38.590
Damn it.

00:13:38.590 --> 00:13:40.600
What a piece of shit.

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:49.630
What do you want?

00:13:49.630 --> 00:13:52.080
Sorry, but I'm Hannah's customer!

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:52.760
What?

00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:54.350
Now, there, Oreld.

00:13:54.510 --> 00:13:55.780
Oh, I see.

00:13:55.780 --> 00:13:57.230
You're the famous...

00:13:58.480 --> 00:13:59.720
Don't worry, my dear.

00:13:59.720 --> 00:14:02.010
I'll take care of things.

00:14:02.010 --> 00:14:05.490
I'll take care of everything for you, Hannah.

00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:09.330
Oreld!

00:14:09.330 --> 00:14:10.550
What are you doing?!

00:14:10.550 --> 00:14:11.880
Scum!

00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:12.880
Hey!

00:14:12.880 --> 00:14:14.150
Stop it!

00:14:14.150 --> 00:14:16.130
Someone, someone come here!

00:14:16.130 --> 00:14:17.540
That'll be enough, kiddo.

00:14:18.010 --> 00:14:19.280
Don't interfere with me!

00:14:19.280 --> 00:14:21.100
Save your energy, boy.

00:14:24.660 --> 00:14:26.090
Damn, that hurts.

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:29.220
Gosh, that was a big mess you've caused.

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:30.680
Sorry.

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:32.750
I just got angry and...

00:14:32.750 --> 00:14:35.930
But, where'd you pick up those bouncers?

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:38.920
There's a lot of relentless people like you,

00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:40.460
so I need to hire people like them.

00:14:41.530 --> 00:14:44.740
I just wanted Hannah to smile.

00:14:46.590 --> 00:14:48.940
I wanted her to smile from her heart.

00:14:50.210 --> 00:14:51.870
Don't get too conceited.

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:54.470
You want to make Hannah smile?

00:14:54.470 --> 00:14:56.950
You think you can do that?

00:14:56.950 --> 00:14:58.650
You have that ability in you?

00:14:59.070 --> 00:15:00.300
Now, that's funny.

00:15:00.300 --> 00:15:01.670
You can't accomplish that.

00:15:02.650 --> 00:15:04.160
Neither can I.

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:06.380
No one can.

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:11.520
Hannah will smile from her heart when her boyfriend comes back...

00:15:13.200 --> 00:15:15.570
...as empty as that may be.

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:17.530
The guy's dead already.

00:15:17.530 --> 00:15:18.490
He's dead?

00:15:19.840 --> 00:15:23.570
One letter that informed her "your boyfriend is dead"...

00:15:23.570 --> 00:15:26.400
Who would accept that?!

00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:30.450
Of course, she wouldn't accept that!

00:15:30.800 --> 00:15:31.630
Right?!

00:15:33.030 --> 00:15:34.900
He was killed in action?

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:36.640
That's how it is.

00:15:37.180 --> 00:15:39.310
Her heart is forever shut.

00:15:40.920 --> 00:15:43.040
Leave her alone if you understand.

00:15:44.100 --> 00:15:46.210
That's what it means to be considerate.

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:56.430
A woman that keeps on waiting, huh?

00:15:58.050 --> 00:16:03.420
There's a woman... that's still waiting for
a man that went to the war to come back.

00:16:04.200 --> 00:16:06.790
The problem is he's dead.

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:11.090
Why does she have to think about a dead guy so much?

00:16:12.510 --> 00:16:15.670
To the point of becoming an empty shell, even.

00:16:18.190 --> 00:16:20.410
But I can't leave her alone,

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:24.240
even though it's not like there's something I can do.

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:30.550
I think it's because it's not over yet.

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:34.430
The war is not over yet.

00:16:35.130 --> 00:16:37.010
So, nobody can move on.

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:39.120
I was like that, too.

00:16:39.880 --> 00:16:43.530
I couldn't accept the fact the war was over.

00:16:44.580 --> 00:16:48.820
But, lately, I've been able to acknowledge that notion.

00:16:49.580 --> 00:16:51.170
Bit by bit, though.

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:53.150
It was after I joined Section III.

00:16:55.010 --> 00:16:56.640
So, I'm sure she's...

00:17:00.050 --> 00:17:02.560
It's not over yet, huh?

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:06.790
Note: "Militärischer Bericht" is German for "Military Report"
"Kaiserliche Armee" is German for "Imperial Army"

00:17:42.100 --> 00:17:43.200
Don't worry.

00:17:43.570 --> 00:17:44.920
I will be back.

00:17:47.950 --> 00:17:48.820
I will.

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:51.390
I promise you.

00:18:02.650 --> 00:18:03.700
Frank!

00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:05.060
You came back?

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:06.240
Frank!

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:14.030
Neugelitz was a battle that would decide the outcome of the war back then.

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:19.020
The Republic planned to strike
the Imperial City right after taking Neugelitz.

00:18:19.880 --> 00:18:25.410
The Imperial forces at Neugelitz were low on men and equipment.

00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:26.620
Stop...

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:28.860
The Empire sent reinforcements from the Imperial City,

00:18:28.860 --> 00:18:29.470
Please, stop!
The Empire sent reinforcements from the Imperial City,

00:18:29.470 --> 00:18:29.820
Please, stop!

00:18:29.820 --> 00:18:30.710
the troops that were sent included the 7th Company-
Please, stop!

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:32.750
the troops that were sent included the 7th Company-

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:34.140
Stop!!!

00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:36.350
Frank is not dead!

00:18:37.590 --> 00:18:39.300
There's no way he'd die...

00:18:41.090 --> 00:18:42.460
Why is that?

00:18:42.460 --> 00:18:44.840
Why do you not try to understand it?

00:18:44.840 --> 00:18:47.050
He fought with his life...

00:18:47.050 --> 00:18:48.430
...for this country...

00:18:48.430 --> 00:18:49.770
...to protect you...

00:18:51.290 --> 00:18:52.690
You must listen, Hannah.

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:54.960
You must know with what feelings he fought the war...

00:18:54.960 --> 00:18:57.200
...what feelings he died with...

00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:59.570
...so that you can live his part, as well.

00:19:06.090 --> 00:19:11.230
The 7th Company departed the Imperial City and arrived at Neugelitz on February 5th.

00:19:11.690 --> 00:19:14.340
The forces there were nearly all wiped out.

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:19.010
The Republic had three battalions, including one tank battalion.

00:19:19.530 --> 00:19:21.730
In a temperature of -15 degrees Celsius,

00:19:21.730 --> 00:19:24.090
the battleplan the 7th Company adopted was...

00:19:24.090 --> 00:19:26.790
...an exhaustive trench warfare.

00:19:26.790 --> 00:19:29.300
Without regard for the serious disadvantage,

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:31.150
they continued to fight.

00:19:31.860 --> 00:19:33.600
Their supplies would run out three days later, though.

00:19:34.720 --> 00:19:36.530
They did consider retreat,

00:19:36.530 --> 00:19:38.660
but without knowing that reinforcements were on the way,

00:19:38.660 --> 00:19:40.910
the 7th Company continued to fight.

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:44.980
Five days later, half of the men died from hunger and frost.

00:19:45.380 --> 00:19:47.650
Yet, they still continued to fight...

00:19:48.130 --> 00:19:50.830
...in order to protect... those they loved.

00:19:59.120 --> 00:20:02.660
Later, the 7th Company would gain a temporary advantage,

00:20:02.660 --> 00:20:04.150
but on February 15th,

00:20:04.150 --> 00:20:08.780
the Republican Army's 3rd Battalion of the 4th Division arrived at Neugelitz.

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:11.890
Suddenly, the 7th Company was at a disadvantage again.

00:20:11.890 --> 00:20:15.800
However, reinforcements were just fifty kilometers away from Neugelitz.

00:20:16.760 --> 00:20:18.140
Just two more days...

00:20:18.140 --> 00:20:21.230
No... if they could hang in there for one more day, there could be a chance of winning the battle.

00:20:21.600 --> 00:20:23.360
By betting all their chances on this,

00:20:23.720 --> 00:20:25.610
they continued to fight.

00:20:31.030 --> 00:20:33.380
Their ammunition began to run out,

00:20:33.380 --> 00:20:35.980
and only a third of the company was left.

00:20:35.980 --> 00:20:38.130
They just needed to hold for one more day.

00:20:39.240 --> 00:20:44.080
However, already depleted, the 7th Company was completely isolated.

00:20:44.670 --> 00:20:45.470
And...

00:20:46.040 --> 00:20:48.240
At 1400 on February 17th,

00:20:48.880 --> 00:20:50.770
the entire company launched a final attack...

00:21:16.590 --> 00:21:17.760
Heartbroken?

00:21:20.230 --> 00:21:23.090
Me, heartbroken?

00:21:26.250 --> 00:21:27.970
That's not it?

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:31.460
You're all into your work, unlike yesterday.

00:21:31.460 --> 00:21:34.320
What are you guys thinking?!

00:21:34.320 --> 00:21:37.250
I just can't leave those kind of women alone.

00:21:37.250 --> 00:21:38.480
So, it's not about love?

00:21:38.480 --> 00:21:40.040
Of course not.

00:21:40.040 --> 00:21:41.440
I see.

00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:46.550
Everyone's here, right?

00:21:46.550 --> 00:21:50.190
Okay, let's go and give all we've got for war relief!

00:21:56.960 --> 00:21:58.940
I got dumped... eh?

00:23:31.000 --> 00:23:34.140
Mer-kun, do you know the meaning of Pumpkin Scissors?

00:23:34.140 --> 00:23:36.980
The origins to the formation of S.S. III will now be told!

00:23:36.980 --> 00:23:37.990
Please look forward to it!

00:23:38.850 --> 00:23:40.920
Next time, "Pumpkins and Scissors".

00:23:40.920 --> 00:23:43.070
Come get us if you're not scared!
